--- surface summary ---
Native WinUI 3 / .NET 10 parity port of web components/ai/AIVoiceMode.tsx, composed with the shared
AIFeatureCard scaffold + the withAiFeature gate. Files (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/):
  AIVoiceMode.Model.cs      - registration + i18n keys/fallbacks, stream-state/event/error enums,
                              AiVoiceStreamEvent (+factories), AiVoiceRequest {message,session_id},
                              AiVoiceSseParser (port of parseSSEFrame/toTypedEvent), VoiceSentenceChunker
                              (port of popCompleteSentences), AIVoiceModeDiagnostics. (WinUI-free, Windows-free)
  AIVoiceMode.Source.cs     - IAiVoiceStreamTransport + HttpAiVoiceStreamTransport (port of useAiStream over
                              fetch+ReadableStream); ISpeechDictation / ISpeechPlayback / ITranscriptDraftStore
                              ports + Unavailable/Silent/Null defaults. (WinUI-free, Windows-free; reuses the
                              shared IAiFeatureGate)
  AIVoiceMode.ViewModel.cs  - INotifyPropertyChanged state holder: gate, transcript, listening, TTS on/off,
                              stt error, stream lifecycle, sentence-chunked speech, all localized labels + a11y
                              names + the {message,session_id} body with a stable per-instance session id.
  AIVoiceMode.cs            - WinUI ContentControl view + WinRT speech adapters (WindowsSpeechDictation over
                              Windows.Media.SpeechRecognition, WindowsSpeechPlayback over
                              Windows.Media.SpeechSynthesis+MediaPlayer) + ApplicationData draft store.

Data sources (P1/S8 state-holder seam, no HTTP in the view): useTranslation -> ILocalizer facade;
useAiStream -> IAiVoiceStreamTransport (POST /api/v1/ai/voice/chat, SSE). On-device speech recognition +
synthesis are device ports; only transcribed text is sent, never raw audio (web contract).

States reproduced (every branch asserted headlessly): gate-off (collapsed, no automation id) | idle with
empty hint | listening (live transcript region hint) | dictation error | dictation-unavailable hint |
streaming/thinking skeleton (reduced-motion aware) | accumulating reply text | done | error (Helix error
message) | offline (connectivity-aware message) | confirm-pause | cancel. Controls: mic start/stop, mute/
unmute spoken replies, stop-all while busy. TTS speaks one complete sentence at a time via the chunker.

i18n: all 20 translation.voiceMode.* keys resolve from Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw; the shared
helix.* / ai.common.* AIFeatureCard keys resolve via the English fallback (same as the sibling AI surfaces);
common.offline is present in the catalog. No English string literals in native code.

Accessibility: Narrator names on the transcript live region and every interactive control (mic / TTS / stop /
Ask Helix), the badge and the surface root; reduced-motion-aware thinking skeleton; live-region announce on
the transcript + output. Telemetry: view.opened slug=AIVoiceMode (PII-safe) emitted once on load.

